WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.600
I have built 19 companies. One of them I

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:05.040
sold for a huge amount of money to Price

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.520
Waterhouse Cooper. I've actually

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.960
invested in over 85 companies as well.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.719
So if you want to start a business, all

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.400
I need you to do is just settle in for

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:13.599
20 minutes. [music] Get a notepad. I'm

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.880
going to teach it all to you for free.

00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:17.359
What have you got to lose? So let's get

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.760
started.

00:00:17.359 --> 00:00:21.680
So there are eight basic principles that

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:23.680
you need to know to start a business.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.439
And the first one will surprise you. You

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:29.279
don't need an idea or money to start a

00:00:25.439 --> 00:00:31.039
business. What you need is a purpose. A

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:32.880
problem in the world that bothers you.

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:35.760
What is it in the world that bothers you

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:39.120
that needs fixing? A purpose, a problem

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:41.280
you've experienced can lead to a great

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.200
business. Why? Because it matters to

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.680
you. I recently invested in a business

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:48.079
called Lovable. It's just hit 10 billion

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:50.239
in valuation. And when Anton pitched

00:00:48.079 --> 00:00:52.640
that business to me a long time ago, he

00:00:50.239 --> 00:00:55.120
said, "Simon, my friends kept asking me

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.000
to help them code their apps. They kept

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.600
asking me to be their CTO and I can't.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.000
I'm doing something else. But I wanted

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.920
to help my friends out. So, he built a

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.000
product to basically help his friends

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.840
out. They kept asking him for help. It

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.430
allows you to tell the app what you want

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.799
it to build and it builds it for you.

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:12.799
[music] And the reason I tell you this

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:14.720
story is because ultimately the lesson

00:01:12.799 --> 00:01:17.200
to learn here is that you [laughter]

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:19.759
have to do it. You don't want it to

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.920
succeed. You need it to succeed. But

00:01:19.759 --> 00:01:25.119
it's important for a business to really

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:28.640
be sustainable for it to have a purpose

00:01:25.119 --> 00:01:31.119
beyond just making money. And so often

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:33.680
your purpose is found in your pain. So

00:01:31.119 --> 00:01:35.200
again for me I was suddenly in the real

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.280
world at 15, [music]

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.119
couldn't get a job, couldn't get help

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.759
from social services. So I had to start

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:45.200
a business, right? And I managed it. And

00:01:41.759 --> 00:01:46.640
now here I am 37 years later wanting to

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.240
give that knowledge to you, right?

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:50.880
That's my pain. I want to give that

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.560
15-year-old me help to start a business

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.159
because I didn't know how to do it. And

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.920
maybe if you don't know your purpose,

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:57.920
let's move on to ideas for a second

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.600
because I can help you think of an idea

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.240
that maybe link back to purpose in a

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:04.320
minute. The second step in starting a

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:07.360
business that so many people put first

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:09.119
is an idea. So what is the idea? The

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:12.560
idea you start with doesn't have to be

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:14.480
the end business. So my first idea when

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.319
I was 15 years old was a gardening

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.080
company. And today I'm one of the

00:02:16.319 --> 00:02:19.680
biggest business influencers in the

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.959
world on social media. So where you end

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.440
up doesn't have to be where you start,

00:02:20.959 --> 00:02:25.599
but you have to start. So an idea as

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:28.000
simple as, and you won't like it. Go

00:02:25.599 --> 00:02:30.000
wash cars. Go wash windows. Learn to

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.520
sell to people. Learn to get a customer.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.280
Learn to make that customer happy. Learn

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:35.519
to hire people. That's what happened to

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.280
me at 15. My first business didn't have

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:40.000
a purpose, by the way. That's why it

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:42.160
eventually failed. But it did have I

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.000
needed money and therefore I went and

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.519
tried things and I had nothing to lose

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:47.840
because I couldn't get a job. I was

00:02:45.519 --> 00:02:50.239
homeless. I had no choice. The best

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:53.599
thing you can do is tell yourself, I've

00:02:50.239 --> 00:02:55.440
got no ego. I I don't care if I fail. I

00:02:53.599 --> 00:02:57.120
don't care if people judge me, but I'm

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.400
going to try stuff. Let's assume you

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.920
haven't got purpose, but you can figure

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.920
it out later. Let's assume you have got

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.840
an idea. What's the next step once

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.367
you've got an idea? Starting your own

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:07.040
business is like moving a mountain.

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:08.879
[music] Don't look at the mountain and

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:10.239
think, "How can I move this mountain?"

00:03:08.879 --> 00:03:12.400
Because you might not even start. You

00:03:10.239 --> 00:03:13.680
might get totally intimidated. Instead,

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.280
think like the Japanese. And the

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:18.480
Japanese have a saying to move a

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:21.280
mountain, move one small rock at a time.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:23.680
So, you have an idea. It might be a big

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:26.800
mountain. What's the first rock? In my

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:29.280
opinion, it's naming the baby. Come up

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:31.360
with a name for the business. Now, many

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:33.680
years ago, I started a business called

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:35.519
Fluid. And that business originally was

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:37.040
a brainstorming session between me and

00:03:35.519 --> 00:03:38.879
my co-founder, someone called Helen

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.680
Griffith. And we both came up with a

00:03:38.879 --> 00:03:44.319
name. My name idea was Pink Tank as in

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:46.879
brainy think tank, right? And her idea

00:03:44.319 --> 00:03:48.400
was fluid. And just by discussing the

00:03:46.879 --> 00:03:49.840
name, we came up with why the business

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.560
should be called Fluid and not Pink

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:55.440
Tank. Point I'm making is naming the

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.840
baby allows you to have expectation that

00:03:55.440 --> 00:04:00.319
the baby will arrive and it gives you a

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:02.080
framework to build everything up. What

00:04:00.319 --> 00:04:03.920
does the brand stand for? Just as

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:05.840
important, what does the brand stand

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:07.840
against? And if you can figure that out

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:10.400
by just coming up with a name, you're on

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:14.000
your way. Step number two, idea and name

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.599
it. Name the idea. Third step in

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.479
building a business, assuming now you've

00:04:15.599 --> 00:04:20.720
named it, what do you do? In my opinion,

00:04:18.479 --> 00:04:22.800
it's get the trademark. From all my

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:25.040
years of experience, I once started a

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:28.160
business called Fluid out in China and

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:29.919
it did really well. And as it took off,

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.600
someone else took the trademark [music]

00:04:29.919 --> 00:04:34.080
and suddenly I found myself in a

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:37.120
trademark dispute because most people

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:39.280
think there's three elements to securing

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:40.960
your business name. One is the actual

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:42.240
registered company. Let's call it in

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:44.639
England company's house or wherever it

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:46.320
is LLC in America. You register the

00:04:44.639 --> 00:04:48.880
business, but that does not give you

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:51.120
protection to use that name. You can

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:54.000
have HSBC and many people have named

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:59.360
their company HSBC, but you cannot trade

00:04:54.000 --> 00:05:03.680
publicly with a brand of HSBC unless you

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:05.280
own the trademark. It's so important.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:07.120
You can own the website address

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:09.280
HSBC.com,

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:11.919
but it does not mean you can trade as

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.520
HSBC. You must own the trademark. And

00:05:11.919 --> 00:05:16.080
it's actually very cheap if you get the

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:18.720
trademark early. Most markets around the

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:20.160
world per category it's about $500 US

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:22.080
which in reality I'll give you that

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.280
money. I'll give you that money. If you

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.560
let me know your name down below I'll

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:25.440
pick one of you if I like the name and

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:26.560
I'll give you the money to get the

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:28.880
trademark. The point I'm trying to get

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:29.840
to here is that it's not launch the

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:32.479
business yet. We're going to come to

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:34.080
that in a minute. It's make sure the

00:05:32.479 --> 00:05:35.440
foundation of the business is solid.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.720
You've got a name that relates to your

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:38.560
purpose and your mission, your brand,

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:40.720
and then you've got ownership over that

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:41.840
name. Now you can trademarks will take

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:43.680
about three or four months to get

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.720
approved, maybe longer sometimes. You

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:45.600
can still build up stuff in the

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:47.120
business. I'm going to go through it in

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:49.520
a minute. But I want you to get that

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:51.600
foundation locked in so that when you do

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.199
fully launch, you don't get a seat and

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.479
assist a bit later like I did because

00:05:53.199 --> 00:05:56.320
someone took the trademark of the

00:05:54.479 --> 00:05:58.560
business that I was operating. Right.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:00.479
The fourth thing to do is secure all

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:02.320
your assets such as your social media

00:06:00.479 --> 00:06:03.840
handles and every channel. Again, this

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:05.199
might be a bit of a headache these days

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.880
because people sit on social media

00:06:05.199 --> 00:06:08.639
handles they're not even using, but you

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.919
can report them now. So, for example, an

00:06:08.639 --> 00:06:11.360
X, you can actually report a handle

00:06:09.919 --> 00:06:13.280
that's not being used, and they will

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:15.919
release it to you if you have a business

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:17.600
account. So, get your social handles

00:06:15.919 --> 00:06:19.280
secured for your business. Even if

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:21.360
you're not going to use them, they'll be

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:22.960
useful later. And certainly things like

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:24.960
website purchase and those sorts of

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:26.319
things are really useful for SEO. If

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:28.720
people want to find you by your brand

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:30.880
name a bit later, try and secure it. If

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:33.199
you can secure all your assets for your

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:34.960
name, it will help increase visibility

00:06:33.199 --> 00:06:36.880
over time and it will help with things

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:38.960
like search engine optimization and even

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:40.400
things like AI, search optimization

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:42.560
later, which is going to be a big thing.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:44.319
It will help you get traffic to your

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:46.880
business. The next thing I want to teach

00:06:44.319 --> 00:06:48.560
you, you've got to learn to leverage AI.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:50.720
Right now, there's a big opportunity on

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:52.160
two levels. One is social media. You can

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.280
post a video and get a million views.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:55.840
You can. It's not about how many

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:58.319
followers you have anymore. Point is

00:06:55.840 --> 00:07:01.039
that you must leverage these tools. AI

00:06:58.319 --> 00:07:02.400
in particular right now can be your CFO.

00:07:01.039 --> 00:07:04.400
Like I just mentioned about lovable, it

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:07.120
can build your site for you. My sponsor

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:08.960
for today's video is build your store AI

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.479
and you can literally go to the link

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:12.560
down below, click another button that

00:07:10.479 --> 00:07:14.880
says get started and build a Shopify

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:16.400
store in minutes. And in addition to

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:18.639
that, if you don't know what product to

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:20.960
sell, it will help you pick what

00:07:18.639 --> 00:07:22.400
products you could sell. I suggest you

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:24.319
pick things that actually matter to you.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:26.479
You should just try it. For me, these

00:07:24.319 --> 00:07:28.560
sorts of products are exactly what the

00:07:26.479 --> 00:07:30.560
wealthy do. They learn to leverage tools

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:32.319
like AI instead of being scared of it

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:34.160
and running away from it and not

00:07:32.319 --> 00:07:35.680
realizing they can actually help you get

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:36.800
where you want to be. Of course, no one

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:39.759
knows what's going to happen in the

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:42.080
future, but right now these tools can

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:43.680
give you a chance to go out there and

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:46.240
build the life you want. Why would you

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:48.720
not try it? Learn to use them. The next

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:51.919
thing we need to do [music] is sell

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:53.120
something. Anything. When I was 15 years

00:07:51.919 --> 00:07:55.039
old and I started the gardening

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:56.845
business, I knocked on the door and I

00:07:55.039 --> 00:07:59.840
asked to tidy up someone's garden

00:07:56.845 --> 00:08:02.560
[music] and they said yes. Now, as I was

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:04.800
tidying up the garden, I also noticed

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:06.800
that their house was in a little bit of

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:08.400
disarray as well. Now, at the time, my

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:09.919
brain wasn't mature enough to realize I

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:13.199
could have sold a second thing. I could

00:08:09.919 --> 00:08:14.960
have sold the fix your house up service,

00:08:13.199 --> 00:08:16.879
but I didn't. But I remember thinking at

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:18.479
the time, these people have a lot of

00:08:16.879 --> 00:08:20.879
money. It's a big house in a very

00:08:18.479 --> 00:08:22.400
expensive area. Why the hell have their

00:08:20.879 --> 00:08:23.759
is their house a little bit run down? It

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:26.720
was the same reason their garden was run

00:08:23.759 --> 00:08:28.960
down. And it's called market fit. If you

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:31.280
have a painting that you've done and

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:32.800
someone will actually buy it, you can

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:34.719
prove there's a market for your

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:36.640
services. And you need to do the numbers

00:08:34.719 --> 00:08:38.560
game most of the time, but you need to

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:40.640
make sure you get one sale. That one

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:42.479
person you sell to can tell 10 people

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:44.560
and help do the sales for you. But what

00:08:42.479 --> 00:08:45.920
I'm trying to teach you is you have to

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.440
sell. Now, if you're an introvert and

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:50.240
you're listening to this thinking, "I

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:53.120
